{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact 391d20cd673c51aac21e7d9e64a1e1ea65e75116 for the intermediate verifier request 42342e35a7660b466b3f623309702461e8f44f6f / builder promise 4e66accc560de6f8ca320ee24593cb0df4f63448. Normal read-only preparation assigns this delivery solely to that fresh implementation request and examines all 46 artifacts, with primary db1ec1fbc69692ccd5779507e8124d7582b0dff3 first. Invitation 9122c446 / checker promise f5c48aee is the review commitment. This does not satisfy original Stage 3 1e8fee4b / 3af8ebc7, any other stage, a main landing, deployment, or first-Jam readiness.\n\nP2 — Report the checks actually made when semantic replay is disabled.\npackages/log/src/cli.ts:17,31 selects replayDecisions:false for --no-replay. packages/log/src/verify.ts:531,1222–1233,1434 skips semantic replay, checkCarry and derived call-session comparisons. Nevertheless cannotProve at 262,265–266,270 unconditionally says policy decisions and recorded carry judgments were replayed, v2 calls/inputs derived and duplicate/newer judgments detected. carryAccounting remains \"partial\" at 1527; CLI:44–45 prints those claims and JSON exports them unchanged. A count of zero decisions does not explain that the invocation omitted these checks.\n\nActual distinguishing evidence uses one signed published log with a duplicated check-carried event at entry 26. The same published head d45a5e2652b9226edb7706bdc3ba695973476e6a is read by all four public CLI invocations. Default JSON and text exit 1: decision-extra at 26, verified through 25. --no-replay JSON and text exit 0: ok:true, verified through 26, decisionsReplayed:0, no failures/limits, but retain the unconditional replay/duplicate claims. This proves false disclosure; deliberately supporting an integrity-only option is not itself the defect.\n\nRepair the common report so machine and human consumers can identify the selected verification mode and proof strength, and so every positive policy/carry/input/g