gacy behavior are expressly within this intermediate commission.\n\nSupported default behavior and scope.\nIndependent source review covered the complete delivered verifier, decoder, historical vocabulary, fold, roster/authority, obligations, derived call session, CLI, protocol/release sections and dated carry-accounting argument. Default mode selects D(s) before each entry; distinguishes undeclared kinds, binding/body/target/historical actor, legacy versus declared semantics, retained policy versions and unsupported profile/steps; derives delivered admission and recorded system evaluation calls/inputs and compares their budget under the applicable evaluation session. Recorded check carries are independently qualified where supported, with duplicate/newer-check/open-blocking-obligation guards. Present preparation facts and Git objects qualify relevant checks; missing Git/prepared facts, receipt effects/platform transitions and the Stage 6 remainder stay disclosed. There is no new default semantic evaluator change in this seven-path log/protocol delta relative to 9451.\n\nWhole-log legacy witnesses were actually loaded. The honest v1 recovery sequence through v2 activation and recover release passed all original assertions through 11, with two decisions replayed and no failures/limits. The intentionally wrong v2-vocabulary module graph passed the required negative: first signed v1 claim at 2 is binding-stale and verification stops through 1. These provide bounded positive/negative legacy credit, not a complete mutation inventory. Successful and failing JSON/text default captures retain the complete partial-carry disclosure and prefix limits. The history-rewrite fixture reports the independently verified predecessor at published/verified 2; it does not certify the rewritten entry. The duplicate fixture independently distinguishes published 26 from verified 25.\n\nThe dated omission argument supports only the source-qualified deletion case: deleting a negative judgment